<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ala ad-Din Muhammad II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1200">1200</a>–<a href="/years/1220">1220</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ala ad-Din Muhammad II was the shah of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmian-empire">Khwarazmian Empire</a> from 1200 to 1220. He expanded his realm across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, making it one of the largest states in the Islamic world. His provocation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, including the killing of Mongol envoys and merchants, brought a devastating Mongol invasion, and he died in flight in 1220 or soon afterwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ala-ad-din-muhammad-ii.jpg" alt="Ala ad-Din Muhammad II" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jami' al-tawarikh, Rashid al-Din, 15th century · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muhammad_II_portrait_in_a_1430_manuscript_of_the_Jami%27_al-tawarikh_by_Rashid-al-Din_Hamadani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
